2026-09-20 23:11:00 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\n        You are a workflow assistant. Extract parameters for the intent "select_idea_by_reference".\n\n        User message:\n        select this: 24-109 louisiana v callais\n\n        Parameter schema for this intent:\n        - "reference": type=string, required=True\n\n        Extraction instructions for this intent:\n        - The "reference" parameter must always be set to the idea\'s "id" field.\n- Never return the idea name or description.\n- Use the relevant context block (which lists ideas with id, name, and description)\n  to determine which idea the user is referring to.\n- If the user refers to an idea by name, description, or position (e.g., "the immigration case",\n  "idea 3", "the fed reserve governor case"), resolve it to the correct idea and return its id.\n\n\n\nRelevant context:\nideas:\n  - id: 24-1260, name: Watson v. RNC, description: The case is about whether Congress in 1845 blocked states from receiving ballots cast on Election Day after that day, a practice allowed for over a century and respected by Congress until now. The issue is whether setting the federal Election Day applies the same rules as in 1845, which would invalidate modern voting methods and state laws. The dispute centers on the interpretation of Election Day statutes.\n  - id: 24-109, name: Louisiana v. Callais, description: The case concerns a dispute over Louisiana\'s congressional map, with the state arguing that it was forced to draw its own map due to a federal court\'s potential interference in the upcoming election, and seeking reversal of a lower court\'s decision on grounds of standing, racial predominance, and the good reasons inquiry.\n  - id: 23-370, name: Erlinger v. United States, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether a judge can increase a defendant\'s sentencing range based on conduct not previously found by a jury, or if the Sixth Amendment requires a more specific factual inquiry.\n  - id: 24-304, name: Laboratory Corp. of America v. Davis, description: This case is about whether a class action lawsuit can proceed when some of the plaintiffs do not have the legal right to bring their claim, and whether courts must first determine if they have jurisdiction over each plaintiff before considering the merits of the case.\n  - id: 23-175, name: City of Grants Pass v. Johnson, description: The case City of Grants Pass v. Johnson, docket number 23-175, concerns the constitutionality of camping laws in public spaces and whether they can be enforced to address growing encampments, with the Ninth Circuit\'s ruling being challenged by the city.\n  - id: 21-1168, name: Mallory v. Norfolk Southern Railway Co., description: The case is about whether Pennsylvania\'s consent-by-registration statute complies with the Constitution, specifically the Fourteenth Amendment, and whether it unfairly favors large corporations over individual citizens.\n  - id: 24-568, name: Bost v. IL Bd. of Elections, description: The case Bost v. IL Bd. of Elections concerns whether Illinois can count mail-in ballots received up to two weeks after Election Day, with the Petitioners arguing that this is too long and could affect a congressional election.\n  - id: 20-255, name: Mahanoy Area School Dist. v. B. L., description: The case centers on whether the landmark Supreme Court decision Tinker applies to speech that occurs off school grounds, particularly on social media, and whether schools can restrict such speech without infringing on students\' First Amendment rights.\n  - id: 19-465, name: Chiafalo v. Washington, description: The case, Chiafalo v. Washington, centers on whether states have the power to control how electors vote in presidential elections, with the Constitution\'s design and language being key factors in determining this issue.\n  - id: 22-210, name: Dupree v. Younger, description: The Supreme Court is deciding whether a party must reargue a legal issue at trial to preserve it for appeal, or if the issue is automatically preserved after a summary judgment ruling.\n  - id: 19-8709, name: Greer v. United States, description: The case Greer v. United States concerns the method an appellate court uses to review a defendant\'s trial, specifically whether it can rely on information not presented at the original trial when affirming a conviction.\n  - id: 18-776, name: Guerrero-Lasprilla v. Barr, description: The case concerns the scope of judicial review over questions of law decided by the Board of Immigration Appeals, specifically whether courts can review whether the government used the proper legal standard in making decisions.\n  - id: 19-1257, name: Brnovich v. Democratic National Committee, description: The case is about whether Arizona\'s voting laws deny minority voters an equal opportunity to cast their votes, despite being eligible and registered to vote.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
